sequenceDiagram
    actor User
    participant CLI as Command-Line Interface
    participant Pipeline as Processing Orchestrator
    participant Cache as Local Cache Database
    participant YouTube as YouTube Extraction Layer
    participant Generator as Study Material Generator
    participant Provider as AI Provider Abstraction
    participant Disk as Output Artifacts

    User->>CLI: notewise process <URL>
    CLI->>Pipeline: submit video identifier(s)
    Pipeline->>Cache: check for existing cached result
    alt Already processed and artifacts complete
        Cache-->>Pipeline: cached match found
        Pipeline-->>User: skip video, reuse existing output
    else Not cached or forced reprocessing
        Pipeline->>YouTube: fetch video metadata and chapters
        YouTube-->>Pipeline: title, duration, chapter markers
        Pipeline->>YouTube: fetch transcript
        YouTube-->>Pipeline: transcript text and language
        Pipeline->>Generator: generate study notes from transcript
        Generator->>Generator: chunk transcript if too long
        loop for each chunk or chapter
            Generator->>Provider: request generation
            Provider-->>Generator: generated text and usage
        end
        Generator->>Generator: stitch chunk outputs into final document
        Generator-->>Pipeline: completed notes (and quiz, if requested)
        Pipeline->>Disk: render and write requested formats
        Pipeline->>Cache: persist transcript, tokens, cost, timings
        Pipeline-->>User: report success, cost, and output paths
    end
